        "Herzog College, 'Midrash Aggadat Bereshit' (research page): The midrash 'was probably created in the ninth century in southern Italy'.",
        "Teugels, 'The Provenance of Aggadat Bereshit: A reassessment of the origins of the work as a Tanchuma satellite' (Brill 2021), PThU record: Record only, with no abstract; keywords include 'Byzantium'. The chapter reassesses its origin as a Tanhuma satellite." ;
    skos:note "Herr (EJ) dates the editing to about the 10th century on grounds of style and anti-Christian polemic, while others (Herzog College, Sefaria) say the 9th century; its provenance (southern Italy or Byzantium, as a 'Tanhuma satellite') is under reassessment (Teugels 2021)."@en ;
