        "Wikipedia (English), 'Numbers Rabbah' (Jewish Encyclopedia-based): Zunz says it is hardly older than the 12th century, and the EJ also gives the 12th century; it was unknown to Nathan b. Jehiel and Rashi but cited by Nahmanides; the two parts differ in origin." ;
    skos:note "The two parts differ in date and origin: Part II is a 9th-century Tanhuma-type midrash, while Part I is late (Zunz: hardly before the 12th century) and depends on Moses ha-Darshan; the two were joined by a copyist around the start of the 13th century."@en ;
    skos:scopeNote "חלק ב' (פרשות 15–23) הוא חומר תנחומא (ממוצא ארץ-ישראלי); חלק א' (פרשות 1–14) בנוי על מדרש ר' משה הדרשן מנרבונה (פרובנס), ולא נקבע מקום עריכתו" ;
    time:hasBeginning opp:dating_Bamidbar_Rabbah_begin ;
