    skos:editorialNote "Encyclopaedia Judaica, 'Genesis Rabbati' (J. Elbaum), on Encyclopedia.com: Usually ascribed to Moses ha-Darshan of Narbonne (first half of the 11th century); published from the only extant manuscript by Albeck (Jerusalem, 1940); Epstein (followed by Albeck) held it is an abridgment of 'the large Genesis Rabbah', which was the work of an anthologist who used some of Moses' work.",
        "Sefaria, 'Bereshit Rabbati' (About this text): Often attributed to 11th-century R. Moshe HaDarshan; may have been compiled by a later editor.",
        "Wikipedia (English), 'Moshe ha-Darshan': Moses ha-Darshan c. early 11th century, head of the yeshiva of Narbonne; Zunz holds the midrash was his work, Epstein that its final compiler was 'certainly not Moses ha-Darshan'." ;
    skos:note "Zunz attributed it to Moses ha-Darshan himself, while Epstein and Albeck see it as an abridgment by a later anonymous compiler who used Moses' work (no firm date for that final compilation was found in the sources seen)."@en ;
    skos:scopeNote "נרבונה – בית מדרשו של ר' משה הדרשן (מחצית ראשונה של המאה ה-11)" ;
