        "Seforim Blog, 'Lekah Tov – What's in a Name?': Written after 1097 (refers to Crusade tribulations); author's residence variously given as Kastoria or Ashkenaz (Mainz suggested by Singer and Seligsohn).",
        "Wikipedia (English), 'Tobiah ben Eliezer' (incorporating the Jewish Encyclopedia): Written in 1097 and revised in 1107 or 1108; covers the Pentateuch and the Five Megillot; Buber proved the author a native of Kastoria." ;
    skos:note "The date is anchored by the work's own allusions to 1096/1097 and a revision of 1107/8 (Sefaria gives c. 1105–1115); the author's place (Kastoria/Balkans vs. Mainz) has been disputed."@en ;
    skos:scopeNote "ר' טוביה בן אליעזר, יליד קסטוריה שבבלקן (בובר); יש שהציעו אשכנז (מגנצא)" ;
