        "Wikipedia (English), 'Midrash Shmuel (aggadah)' (cites Strack & Stemberger 1991): The compiler lived in the Land of Israel; Zunz put him in the first half of the 11th century, which Buber refuted; Strack & Stemberger argue for composition well before the 11th century with later revision." ;
    skos:note "Zunz (followed by EJ) dated it no earlier than the 11th century, but Buber refuted Zunz's arguments, and Strack & Stemberger (via English Wikipedia) hold that it was composed well before the 11th century and later revised, since Samuel b. Hofni and Nissim Gaon cite it."@en ;
