    skos:editorialNote "Encyclopaedia Judaica, 2nd ed., 'Tanhuma Yelammedenu' (Marc Bregman), on Encyclopedia.com: Calls Tanhuma Buber (first published Vilna 1875) 'a European (Italian-Ashkenazi) recension of similar midrashic material'; gives no exact date.",
        "Wikipedia (English), 'Midrash Tanhuma' (cites Townsend 1989; Bregman 2003): Buber dated it to the 5th century, but others disagree; it relies on R. Ahai's mid-8th-century She'iltot (Townsend); Bregman places its origin in Lombard northern Italy, and others favour southern Italy." ;
    skos:note "Buber thought it was a 5th-century Palestinian work older than the Babylonian Talmud, but later scholars reject this: it depends on the mid-8th-century She'iltot (Townsend), and Bregman sees it as a European (Italian-Ashkenazi) recension, while others favour southern Italy."@en ;
    skos:scopeNote "נוסח אירופי (איטלקי-אשכנזי) לפי ברגמן; יש המציעים צפון איטליה (לומברדית) או דרום איטליה" ;
