        "Posen Library, 'What Is Song of Songs Rabbah?': 'Final redaction sometime between the sixth and eighth centuries CE', with a largely Palestinian perspective.",
        "Wikipedia (English), 'Song of Songs Rabbah' (Jewish Encyclopedia-based): The date cannot be fixed exactly; it is later than Pesikta de-Rav Kahana (Theodor) and older than Pesikta Rabbati, hence 'around the end of the 8th century'; Simon Duran calls it a 'Judean aggadic collection'." ;
    skos:note "EJ dates it to about the mid-6th century (its table: 500–640), the Posen Library to between the 6th and 8th centuries, and the Jewish Encyclopedia-based Wikipedia article to the end of the 8th century (reasoning that it predates Pesikta Rabbati, c. 845)."@en ;
    skos:scopeNote "מדרש אמוראי ארץ-ישראלי" ;
