opp:dating_Sifrei_Aggadah_on_Esther a opp:DatingAssertion,
        time:ProperInterval ;
    rdfs:label "רכיבים מהמאה ה-9 בערך עד המאה ה-12"@he ;
    opp:confidence opp:conf_low ;
    dcterms:date "0800/1200" ;
    dcterms:source opp:source_3a7bf7d1ce,
        opp:source_4f0a070828,
        opp:source_54a3b98d8e ;
    dcterms:spatial opp:region_08 ;
    skos:editorialNote "Encyclopaedia Judaica (2007), 'Midrashim, Smaller', on Jewish Virtual Library: Midrash Panim Aherim le-Esther (version A) 'was redacted not earlier than the 12th century', using Esther Rabbah II and Abba Guryon; Buber published it in the Sifrei … Esther.",
        "Sefaria, 'Sifrei Aggadah on Esther' (About This Text): A collection of three midrashim on Esther prepared by Buber: Midrash Abba Gurion, Midrash Panim Aherim and Midrash Lekah Tov. It gives the place as 'Lviv' (Buber's place of work) and no composition date.",
        "Wikipedia (English), 'Midrash Abba Gorion' / EJ 'Midrash Lekah Tov' (JVL): Abba Gorion: 'no later than the ninth century' (Lerner) or 'before 1050' (Academy of the Hebrew Language). EJ (https://www.jewishvirtuallibrary.org/midrash-leka-x1e25-tov) calls Lekah Tov 'a late 11th-century Midrash' whose author lived in the Balkans; its Esther portion was published by Buber in the Sifrei de-Aggadata (1886)." ;
    skos:note "This is Buber's 19th-century collection of three separate midrashim, each dated differently; even for Abba Gurion opinions differ ('no later than the 9th century', per Lerner, versus 'before 1050', per the Academy of the Hebrew Language)."@en ;
    skos:scopeNote "קובץ מודרני של בובר משלושה מדרשים: מדרש אבא גוריון (לא אחרי המאה ה-9 / לפני 1050), פנים אחרים (לא לפני המאה ה-12) ולקח טוב לר' טוביה בן אליעזר (סוף המאה ה-11, הבלקן/ביזנטיון)" ;
    time:hasBeginning opp:dating_Sifrei_Aggadah_on_Esther_begin ;
    time:hasEnd opp:dating_Sifrei_Aggadah_on_Esther_end .

