    skos:editorialNote "Encyclopaedia Judaica, 'Minor Tractates' (A. Rothkoff), on Encyclopedia.com: Some assign the minor tractates to the end of the Geonic period, but recent scholarship favors a much earlier date; Higger: mostly Palestinian, later modified in Babylonia.",
        "M. van Loopik, The Ways of the Sages and the Way of the World (1991), preface/introduction (Mohr Siebeck PDF): Early Derekh Eretz literature dates back to the Tannaitic period, but 'presumably, the final editing did not take place until Gaonitic times'.",
        "Wikipedia (English), 'Derekh Eretz Rabbah' (based on the Jewish Encyclopedia): A contemporary of Rebbi (c. 160–220) may have been the author; sections 1–3 added much later; the Gemara in Coronel's version is very late, probably 10th century." ;
    skos:note "The core may be tannaitic (a contemporary of Rabbi Judah ha-Nasi), but the opening chapters were added much later and van Loopik puts the final editing of the Derekh Eretz tractates in the Geonic period; some older scholars date all the minor tractates to the end of the Geonic period."@en ;
    skos:scopeNote "גרעין תנאי ארץ-ישראלי (לפי היגר רוב המסכתות הקטנות ארץ-ישראליות ועובדו בבבל); תוספות מאוחרות" ;
    time:hasBeginning opp:dating_Tractate_Derekh_Eretz_Rabbah_begin ;
