        "Encyclopaedia Judaica, 'Minor Tractates' (A. Rothkoff), on Encyclopedia.com: Kutim is one of seven brief treatises; Higger: mostly Palestinian, original composition possibly completed by 400 CE; others date them to the end of the Geonic period.",
        "Sefaria, 'Tractate Kutim' (About this text): Composed: Talmudic Israel/Babylon, 750 CE; dating and place are debated." ;
    skos:note "Stemberger dates a friendly core to before the final break with the Samaritans at the end of the 3rd century, while Lehnardt argues that the present text must come from after that break and calls the early dating problematic; Sefaria gives 750 CE."@en ;
    skos:scopeNote "קירכהיים והיגר: מקור ארץ-ישראלי (\"שבע מסכתות קטנות ירושלמיות\"); לנהרדט אינו קובע מקום" ;
