        "Wikipedia (English), 'Yalkut Shimoni' (based on the Jewish Encyclopedia): Author uncertain; Rapoport's 11th-century dating 'untenable'; Epstein inclines to agree with Zunz that the author flourished in the early 13th century; a manuscript known to Azariah dei Rossi existed in 1310." ;
    skos:note "The 13th-century dating (Zunz, Epstein) prevails, but Rapoport put it in the 11th century, Aptowitzer in the mid-12th, and Gaster in 14th-century Spain; the author's identity (Simeon ha-Darshan vs. Simeon Kara) and his Frankfurt origin are also uncertain."@en ;
    skos:scopeNote "מיוחס לר' שמעון הדרשן; לפי Prinz ומסורת יהודי פרנקפורט – מפרנקפורט; צונץ: דרום גרמניה" ;
